		{"id":"legend","type":"text","text":"### Legend\n\nGreen: support for the framing.\nOrange: tension or counter-evidence.\nPurple: deciding evidence and hypotheses.\nEdges label the relationship, not proof.","x":0,"y":0,"width":440,"height":174,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"question","type":"text","text":"### Question\n\nDo short-term symptom gains translate into long-term function, quality of life and safety?","x":990,"y":0,"width":460,"height":116,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"for-0","type":"file","file":"Research/Domains/Pharmacology/Articles/P39701638 Ostinelli 2025 Comparative interventions for ADHD.md","x":0,"y":464,"width":440,"height":200},
		{"id":"guard","type":"text","text":"### Overreach guard\n\nA symptom average is not a life outcome, and an absence of long-term evidence is not evidence of absence.","x":2000,"y":0,"width":440,"height":146,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"deciding","type":"text","text":"### Evidence that would decide\n\nRandomised long-term trials where feasible, and large prospective cohorts that record treatment exposure, functional outcomes and harms with pre-specified confounding control.","x":990,"y":1214,"width":460,"height":174,"color":"6"},
